{"files":[{"content":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    assert(n > 0 && n < 8000 && s > 0 && s < n);\n\n    // Keep only the S rows needed by the vertical sliding window.\n    std::vector<int> row_buffer(static_cast<std::size_t>(s) * n);\n    std::vector<long long> column_sums(n, 0);\n\n    for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n        int* row = row_buffer.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * n;\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n            std::scanf(\"%d\", &row[c]);\n            column_sums[c] += row[c];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long window_sum = 0;\n    for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) window_sum += column_sums[c];\n    long long best = window_sum;\n\n    for (int left = 1; left + s <= n; ++left) {\n        window_sum += column_sums[left + s - 1] - column_sums[left - 1];\n        best = std::max(best, window_sum);\n    }\n\n    for (int top = 1; top + s <= n; ++top) {\n        const int slot = (top - 1) % s;\n        int* row = row_buffer.data() + static_cast<std::size_t>(slot) * n;\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n            int value;\n            std::scanf(\"%d\", &value);\n            column_sums[c] += static_cast<long long>(value) - row[c];\n            row[c] = value;\n        }\n\n        window_sum = 0;\n        for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) window_sum += column_sums[c];\n        best = std::max(best, window_sum);\n        for (int left = 1; left + s <= n; ++left) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[left + s - 1] - column_sums[left - 1];\n            best = std::max(best, window_sum);\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A row-major ring buffer combined with rolling column sums should improve locality and reduce matrix storage from O(N²) to O(SN), while finding the maximum in O(N²) work for every valid size.","notes":"Source-only proposal; no commands were run and no performance or correctness measurements are claimed.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace per-window S-by-S updates with vertical rolling column sums and horizontal sliding sums.","Stream each matrix row once into an S-row ring buffer, updating column sums as departing rows are replaced.","Use contiguous row-major storage and 64-bit accumulators for window sums."]}